! Face-centred-cubic hydrogen at 6.5 bohr: an itinerant ferromagnet cheap
! enough to converge the transverse spin susceptibility on, and the cell the
! P63 identities are measured on.
!
! Three things about it are deliberate.
!
!   * fcc rather than a chain. The kernel of the transverse channel is
!     B_xc(r)/m(r), which grows without bound as the density falls, so a cell
!     with vacuum has an enormous kernel where there is nothing to respond: on
!     a hydrogen chain with 8 bohr between images |B_xc/m| reaches 173 in the
!     tail against 21 in the core, and the leading eigenvalue of X_0 F moves
!     from 1.13 to 0.92 as the density clip moves from 1e-6 to 1e-2. A compact
!     cell has a density ratio of 29 rather than 1858 and the same eigenvalue
!     is stable to the clip.
!   * nosym and noinv with the whole 4x4x4 grid. The states at k + q are read
!     out of this same grid, which needs it closed under translation by q, and
!     X_0(G, G') is a matrix in two G indices that nothing here symmetrises.
!   * a = 6.5 bohr. Below about 6 the cell is not magnetic at all and above it
!     the density ratio climbs; here the moment is 0.53 mu_B, which is an
!     itinerant ferromagnet rather than a set of local moments.
!
! **The ferromagnetic solution is not the ground state and that is why the cell
! is here.** It converges at m = 0.53 mu_B and sits 58 meV *above* the
! nonmagnetic solution of the same input, and the transverse susceptibility says
! so: its leading eigenvalue exceeds one at q = (0, 0, 1/4), which means the
! uniform state is unstable against an infinitesimal spiral of that pitch. No
! lattice constant fixes it -- at 7.0 bohr the ferromagnet is 7 meV below the
! nonmagnetic solution and still soft at finite q, at 8.0 it is fully polarized
! and 64 meV below and still soft -- because a half-filled band on any lattice
! prefers antiferromagnetic order. So this cell is the *identities* case
! (Goldstone, periodicity, the q -> -q reflection), and fcc nickel is the
! physics one. See PLAN.md P63.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 6.5,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.01,
    nspin = 2
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
    starting_magnetization(1) = 1.0
    nbnd = 8
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H 0.0 0.0 0.0
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 4 0 0 0
